    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## JD MANAGEMENT WORKFLOW\n\n**Nodes:** Google Drive JD Trigger → Download JD1 → Extract JD Content1 → Append row in sheet\n\n**Purpose:** Maintains a centralized repository of job descriptions for resume evaluation\n\nJob Desc Google Sheet stores : id, name, text, url\n\n**How it works:**\n- A JD is considered latest based on the last modification field of the document and NOT UPLOADED TO DRIVE TIME\n- Monitors JDs folder for new job descriptions\n- Downloads PDF when new JD is uploaded\n- Extracts text content from PDF\n- Stores in Google Sheets with metadata (id, name, text, url)\n\n**Why needed:** AI Agent requires latest JD text to evaluate resumes accurately\n\n**Without this:** Manual JD updates, outdated evaluations, inconsistent screening criteria\n\n**Optimization:** \n- Automatic extraction eliminates manual copy-paste, ensures single source of truth.\n- Avoids extraction and download of JD for each resume evaluation, reducing compute and latency.",
        "height": 472,
        "width": 862
      },
      "id": "3bff47c7-e910-4e5a-a9fe-32e1adccd42d",
      "name": "Note: JD Management Workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1920,
        -176
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## RESUME PROCESSING WORKFLOW\n\n**Nodes:** Trigger for New Resumes → Search Resumes → Loop Over Resumes → Download Resume → Extract Resume Content -> Evaluation -> Store Results\n\n**Purpose:** Automated resume ingestion and content extraction pipeline\n\n**How it works:**\n- Trigger monitors Resumes folder every minute\n- Search retrieves all resumes with metadata (id, name, webViewLink)\n- Loop processes one resume at a time (batch size: 1)\n- Download fetches PDF only for NEW resumes\n- Extract converts PDF to text for AI analysis\n\n**Why needed:** Enables automated processing without manual intervention\n\n**Without this:** Manual download, copy-paste resume text, human error, slow processing\n\n**Optimization:** Loop ensures sequential processing, prevents API rate limits, maintains data integrity",
        "height": 428,
        "width": 702,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "c1f494e2-0b35-45dd-b9ea-7fde67fe29d2",
      "name": "Note: Resume Processing Workflow",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1344,
        560
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## DUPLICATE DETECTION SYSTEM\n\n**Nodes:** Get Processed Resumes → Handle Empty Sheet → Merge Resume with Processed List → New Resume?\n\n**Purpose:** Prevents reprocessing of already-evaluated resumes (CRITICAL OPTIMIZATION)\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Get Processed Resumes: Fetches all resume_link values from Evaluations sheet\n2. Handle Empty Sheet: Returns NULL if no processed resumes exist (first run scenario)\n3. Merge: Combines current resume metadata with processed list\n4. New Resume?: Checks if webViewLink exists in processed list\n   - TRUE (new) → Download and process\n   - FALSE (duplicate) → Skip to next resume\n\n**Why needed:** Saves bandwidth, API costs, processing time, prevents duplicate entries\n\n**Without this:** Reprocesses same resumes repeatedly, wastes resources, duplicate database entries\n\n**Optimization:** Check happens BEFORE download (saves ~3-6 seconds per duplicate)",
        "height": 416,
        "width": 780,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "536dd3a7-3bd9-4249-b463-97b10d49be99",
      "name": "Note: Duplicate Detection System",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2704,
        1184
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## AI EVALUATION ENGINE\n\n**Nodes:** Get row(s) in sheet → Get Last Row → Merge Resume and JD → AI Agent → Structured Output Parser1 → Google Gemini Chat Model\n\n**Purpose:** Intelligent resume-JD matching with structured, explainable output\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Get row(s): Retrieves all JD records from sheet\n2. Get Last Row: Extracts most recent JD text (Code node)\n3. Merge: Combines resume text + JD text for AI input\n4. AI Agent: Evaluates match with comprehensive system prompt (security guardrails, scoring rules, output format)\n5. Structured Parser: Enforces JSON schema (11 required fields)\n6. Gemini Model: Provides LLM capability (gemini-2.5-flash)\n\n**Why needed:** Objective, consistent, explainable resume screening at scale\n\n**Without this:** Manual screening, subjective bias, inconsistent criteria, slow turnaround\n\n**Optimization:** Structured output ensures data quality, retry logic handles transient failures",
        "height": 416,
        "width": 960,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "f823f34a-fe00-400c-84e0-4c01456dba76",
      "name": "Note: AI Evaluation Engine",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4112,
        128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## DATA PERSISTENCE LAYER\n\n**Nodes:** Append Candidate Details → Loop Over Resumes (feedback)\n\n**Purpose:** Stores evaluation results and enables duplicate detection\n\n**How it works:**\n- Receives structured AI output (11 fields)\n- Appends to Evaluations sheet with timestamp\n- Loops back to process next resume\n- Creates audit trail of all evaluations\n\n**Schema:** candidate_name, candidate_email, candidate_mobile, resume_link, score, justification, strong_points, drawbacks, overall_assessment, screening_stage, processed_timestamp\n\n**Why needed:** Persistent storage, duplicate prevention, reporting, audit trail\n\n**Without this:** No record of evaluations, cannot prevent duplicates, no analytics\n\n**Optimization:** Single append operation per resume, resume_link enables duplicate detection, timestamp tracks processing history",
        "height": 508,
        "width": 556,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "8cbca27d-13d2-489b-b823-aa0a24900a82",
      "name": "Note: Data Persistence Layer",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4512,
        976
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Workflow Architecture\n\n**System Design:** Dual-trigger automated resume screening system  \n**Architecture Pattern:** Event-driven parallel processing with intelligent duplicate detection\n\n### Key Optimizations\n1. Pre-download duplicate check to avoid redundant processing and reduce AI/API costs  \n2. Parallel processing of Job Description retrieval and resume parsing to minimize latency  \n3. Batch handling using Loop node for efficient multi-resume processing  \n4. Strict structured output parsing to ensure data consistency and downstream reliability  \n5. Retry-based error handling for transient AI evaluation failures  \n6. **AI guardrails and safety controls**: constrained prompts, schema-enforced outputs, and prompt-injection resistance to ensure secure, predictable, and explainable AI behavior\n\n### Data Flow\nTrigger → Search → Loop → Duplicate Check → Download → Extract → Merge → AI Evaluate → Store\n\n### Conclusion\nThe system balances automation with safety and human oversight, using AI only where it adds value while enforcing guardrails that maintain trust, reliability, and accountability.\n",
        "height": 508,
        "width": 832,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "a99d0c95-4ea3-4f06-ab76-a7e5d9ab33ca",
      "name": "Note: Workflow Architecture",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2976,
        -256
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Resume Screener\n### Automated Resume Relevance Scoring Workflow\n## **HANVITH SAI ALLA**\n",
        "height": 144,
        "width": 416,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3152,
        -432
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "56c41f1e-35f1-4153-bd37-78d24d799e39",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Future Enhancements, Safety & Advanced Automation\n\n### **Pre-AI Brute-Force Relevance Gate (Cost & Safety Critical)**\n- Apply a **strict deterministic keyword-overlap check** between the Job Description and Resume before invoking AI.  \n- Filter out resumes with **zero or negligible overlap** in mandatory skills, technologies, or domain terms.  \n- Prevents random and irrelevant applications from consuming AI resources while keeping thresholds conservative to avoid false rejections.\n\n---\n\n### Post-Filter Candidate Validation & Enrichment\n- After passing initial filtering, optionally validate profiles using **public professional presence** (LinkedIn, GitHub, portfolios, personal websites).  \n- Cross-check claimed skills and experience; flag inconsistencies for recruiter review (no auto-rejection).\n\n---\n\n### Interview Scheduling Automation\n- Once a recruiter approves a candidate, **automatically analyze recruiter calendar availability** (Google Calendar).  \n- Identify common free slots and generate **proposed interview time windows**.  \n- Email the candidate with selectable time options and confirm the meeting upon response.  \n- Reduces back-and-forth communication and accelerates time-to-interview.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Enhancements & Edge Cases\n- Configurable scoring weights per role (mandatory vs preferred skills)  \n- Recruiter feedback loop to continuously refine evaluations  \n- OCR confidence handling for scanned resumes  \n- Flags for overqualified candidates and keyword stuffing  \n- JD versioning with optional re-evaluation of past candidates  \n\n### These enhancements extend the system from screening to **end-to-end hiring orchestration**, combining safe AI usage, deterministic filtering, and calendar-driven automation to improve recruiter efficiency, candidate experience, and hiring velocity.\n",
        "height": 736,
        "width": 1952,
        "color": 2
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2416,
        1632
      ],
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "id": "a1174647-8731-4bbf-823e-e8ba51286fa5",
      "name": "Sticky Note1"
    }
